{"t": 1794106051.7127018, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline #8812 on `main` (sha `a91c2e0`) is red in the `test:contract` job.\n\nFailure:\n```\ncontract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\n    assert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE   AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\nRoot cause: `billing/invoice.py` built the invoice number with plain string interpolation (`f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`), so the sequence was emitted unpadded (`INV-2026-42`). The FIN-77 Finance ERP import contract requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\nFix (one line in `billing/invoice.py`):\n```python\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerified locally: `python -m pytest contract/ -q` -> `1 passed`. Only the sequence padding changes; the `INV-<year>-` prefix is untouched and sequences of 6 or more digits are not truncated.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
